ts price Vasquez at 94-96%", "Thin, dated polling shows only a narrow 3-point Vasquez lead"], "rationale": "The fundamentals, expert consensus, and markets all point to a Vasquez win, and his large cash advantage reinforces that. The lone recent poll showing just a 3-point margin and the district's even partisan lean argue for keeping the expected margin near the consensus-implied 8 points rather than higher.", "watch": "A late round of public polling showing Cunningham, boosted by Trump's endorsement, closing within a few points would move this toward Lean D.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Gabe Vasquez (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Incumbent Democrat Gabe Vasquez seeks a third term in a southern New Mexico district with an even partisan lean. He holds a clear financial edge, with $2.4 million banked against challenger Greg Cunningham's $0.8 million, and has no outside spending against him. Cunningham has Trump's endorsement, but the national climate favors Democrats this cycle.\n\nMost race raters place the seat at Likely D, with a few at Lean D and one at Safe D, and prediction markets price Vasquez's chances in the mid-90s. The only recent poll, from early September, showed Vasquez up just three points, suggesting the race is not entirely out of reach. The forecast expects Vasquez to win by roughly eight points, consistent with a Likely Democratic rating, with moderate uncertainty given sparse polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8892, "margin": 7.53}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8688, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8708, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.87, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8306, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8384, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8302, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8733, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8614, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8